DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The hhoollee node type silently discards all data and control messages it re‐
     ceives.  This type is used for testing and debugging.

HHOOOOKKSS
     A nngg__hhoollee node accepts any request to connect, regardless of the hook
     name, as long as the name is unique.

CCOONNTTRROOLL MMEESSSSAAGGEESS
     This node type supports the generic control messages, plus the following:

     NGM_HOLE_GET_STATS (ggeettssttaattss)
          This command takes an ASCII string argument, the hook name, and re‐
          turns the statistics associated with the hook as a _s_t_r_u_c_t
          _n_g___h_o_l_e___h_o_o_k_s_t_a_t.

     NGM_HOLE_CLR_STATS (ccllrrssttaattss)
          This command takes an ASCII string argument, the hook name, and
          clears the statistics associated with the hook.

     NGM_HOLE_GETCLR_STATS (ggeettccllrrssttaattss)
          This command is identical to NGM_HOLE_GET_STATS, except that the
          statistics are also atomically cleared.

SSHHUUTTDDOOWWNN
     This node shuts down upon receipt of a NGM_SHUTDOWN control message, or
     when all hooks have been disconnected.

